de your gpa again i  understand that university systems are a  bit different but if you received any  type of numeric gpa i would recommend  you to also include it here on the cv  sometimes people ask me where my gpa  wasn't that strong should i still  include it even if it wasn't that strong  and i'd say yes because at least myself  usually whenever i see a cv without gpa  i just assume that the person doesn't  have such a great gpa right because  otherwise the person would show it on  the cv and then it's always just an  annoyance to needing to look at the  university transcripts maybe that the  person hopefully then attached just look  through all the documents to pull out  the gpas that the person actually has  this is just annoying a waste of time be  transparent include them and of course  ideally what always also helps and you  probably would only include it if really  these numbers are good but if you have a  good also percentage rank so if you can  show that you are part of the top five  top 10 maybe top 15 percent of your  class i would surely include this here  in the cv as well because of course this  helps also the hr professional just to  understand and contextualize the gpa a  little bit better especially maybe if  you're applying from university that  maybe isn't one of the big target  schools where it's a bit less clear on  what the gpa really means whether this  is a good result or not so do you have  any additional tips to share on how to  ride a strong cv so just leave a comment  in the comment section trust you would  all benefit from that if you took any  value out of this video at all please  destroy the like button for the youtube  algorithm and also hit subscribe and  turn on the notification bell to stay up  to date on all my content thank you to  all the members of from learning for  supporting the channel this is very much  appreciated my name is simon i have  these videos every single weekend on  saturdays see you again next week until  